  "findings": [
    "Existing: Root setup, setup-store, attachment verifier and attachment contract equal local main blobs. Reuse these; separate Eve Source lacks these six setup/attachment source/contract/test paths.",
    "Existing: setup-store reads server grant and canonical workspace, enforces owner/revision, explicit quote/recurring consent, billing preparation and runtime receipt. serviceSetupView exposes onboarding state, not full dispatch authorization.",
    "Existing: attachment verifier checks signature, owner, explicit device approval/proof, contract/version, issuer profile, parent epoch, scope, expiry, key/manifest/capability and audience. Tests include eSIM-free child, revoked/stale authority and expiry. Pure verifier is not wired issuer/DB integration evidence.",
    "Missing ESIM-01: combined server decision fixture and explicit product-state matrix across separate telecom/profile/service entitlement/contract/payment/runtime/attachment/job/collection authorities; display active must not authorize dispatch.",
    "Root setup test and cloud access source/test differ from main; cloud access source/test also differ from Eve Source. Integrator must select these diffs; do not copy Source or main over Root.",
    "Keep telecom, SIM profile, owner service rights and OS/client installation independent. No OS binary, LLM, SIM secret or customer content is stored in SIM. Telecom offline alone must not deny otherwise authorized result access/export."
  ],
